<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.12.4: Finding the Missing Data in the Set</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02297</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.12.4: Finding the Missing Data in the Set</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e0c2f858-adce-4f1a-b5a8-dd835c70f1aa</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Thomasina used a quadratic data set to create a curve of best fit for her data. Then she accidentally spilled paint on her paper and lost some of the entries in the table.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-bottom="-100" data-equations="[&quot;y=-.34x^2+30.31x+18.45&quot;]" data-left="-10" data-right="100" data-schema-version="1.0" data-top="800"/>
<para>She needs to work backward to fill in the missing entries in her data set. Use the curve of best fit she created to complete the table.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
      <thead>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(x_1\)
            </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
              \(y_1\)
            </emphasis></entry></row>
          </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry/>
            <entry>
              452.06
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry/>
            <entry>
              632.24
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              58.2
            </entry>
            <entry/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry/>
            <entry>
              176.12
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    
  <para>Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
    <thead>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>
            \(x_1\)
          </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
            \(y_1\)
          </emphasis></entry></row>
        </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry>
            6
          </entry>
          <entry>
            188.07
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            17.9
          </entry>
          <entry>
            452.06
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            31.1
          </entry>
          <entry>
            632.24
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            58.2
          </entry>
          <entry>
            630.83
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            83.6
          </entry>
          <entry>
            176.12
          </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
